 (1475-1507).",null,0,0,null,1,"1/17/Cesare_Borgia_-_Miramare_museum.jpg/330px-Cesare_Borgia_-_Miramare_museum.jpg",0,5,1,0,50,null,null,null,null,48],[139795877,"Jesus Christ bearing the Cross",1530,0,0,null,1,"d/dd/Cristo_portacroce.png/330px-Cristo_portacroce.png",0,1,1,0,null,null,null,null,null,48]],"summaryBase":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/","summaryLicence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","summaryKind":"excerpt","summaryLicenceUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/","factsSource":"Wikidata (CC0)","factsFormat":2,"rankVersion":1,"summaries":{"3714344":["Saint Dorothy or Young Roman Woman with a Fruit Basket is a circa 1512 oil on panel painting by Sebastiano del Piombo, now in the Gemäldegalerie, Berlin. A basket is an attribute of saint Dorothy, hence its first title.","Saint Dorothy (painting)"],"3863235":["The Death of Adonis is a 1512 oil on canvas painting by Sebastiano del Piombo, now in the Uffizi in Florence.","The Death of Adonis (Sebastiano del Piombo)"],"3889258":["The Saint John Chrysostom Altarpiece is an oil painting on canvas of 1510–1511 by Sebastiano del Piombo in the Venetian church of San Giovanni Grisostomo. It belongs to the sacra conversazione genre.","Saint John Chrysostom Altarpiece"],"3904401":["Pietà is an oil on panel painting by Sebastiano del Piombo, executed c. 1516–1517, now in the Museo Civico located in the former cloister of the monastery adjacent to the church of Santa Maria della Verità, Viterbo, region of Lazio, Italy.","Pietà (Sebastiano del Piombo)"],"3907302":["Polyphemus is a circa 1512 fresco by Sebastiano del Piombo in the Villa Chigi, next to Raphael's Triumph of Galatea and continuing its iconography.","Polyphemus (Sebastiano del Piombo)"],"3933578":["The Raising of Lazarus is a large altarpiece of 1517–1519 by the Italian High Renaissance artist Sebastiano del Piombo, for which Michelangelo supplied drawings for some figures.","The Raising of Lazarus (Sebastiano del Piombo)"],"3937680":["Portrait of a Woman is a 1512 oil painting on panel by the Italian painter Sebastiano del Piombo, dated by the artist and now in the Uffizi in Florence.","Portrait of a Woman (Sebastiano del Piombo)"],"3998923":["Detroit Trio, also titled The Appeal, is an oil on canvas painting attributed to Giorgione, Titian and Sebastiano del Piombo, executed c. 1500. It is held now in the Detroit Institute of Arts.","Detroit Trio"],"7232252":["The Portrait of Andrea Doria is a painting finished c. 1526 by the Italian High Renaissance painter Sebastiano Del Piombo. It was painted after Sebastiano had fully mastered his Roman style.","Portrait of Andrea Doria (Sebastiano del Piombo)"],"18397535":["The Judgement of Solomon is an oil on canvas painting by Sebastiano del Piombo of the Judgement of Solomon, executed c. 1505–1510, now in the Bankes collection at Kingston Lacy, a National Trust property in Dorset, England.","The Judgement of Solomon (Sebastiano del Piombo)"],"18397538":["Woman as a Wise Virgin is a circa 1510 oil on canvas painting by Sebastiano del Piombo, now in the National Gallery of Art in Washington.","Woman as a Wise Virgin"],"18397539":["Salome with the Head of John the Baptist or The Daughter of Herodias is a circa 1510 oil on panel painting by Sebastiano del Piombo, now in the National Gallery, London, to which it was left by George Salting in 1910.","Salome with the Head of John the Baptist (Sebastiano del Piombo)"],"21121932":["Pope Paul III with a Nephew is an unfinished 1534 oil on slate portrait by Sebastiano del Piombo, now in the Galleria nazionale di Parma.","Pope Paul III with a Nephew"]},"titlesFrom":["fr","P1476","alias:en","alias:fr","aliasFilter:1"]}